# Shared Path Regression

Changing a shared module is not a single-feature change. Find and verify every consumer before considering the work done.

## Must do

- Search for subclasses, wrappers, and call sites of the touched API, controller, hook, or service.
- Run unit/integration tests for **each consumer area**, not only the feature you meant to change.
- An empty happy path is not enough when filters/params are optional — exercise at least one non-empty path.
- Shared caches / action labels used by multiple callers with different params must not thrash (one shared key, or separate labels/caches).

```text
❌ BAD: Optimize a shared loader and test only the screen you were editing.
✅ GOOD: Also verify every other screen/API that mounts the same shared path.

❌ BAD: Two fetches with different params sharing one cache key or action label.
✅ GOOD: One shared params key per load, or separate labels/caches.
```
